 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with pauses of 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds before
+successive retries. After the final timeout, the error propagates to the caller. See the
+[capture implementation](../../larder/capture.py).
+
+The gateway's Friday peak caused 58 confirmed pantry orders to go uncharged, requiring a volunteer to capture them
+by hand. The previous three attempts ran back to back within a second, all during the same slowdown. A sandbox
+replay with the longer retry window recovered 57 of those 58 captures. The pauses add up to 20 seconds to the
+member's wait on the confirmation page, a trade-off accepted to reduce manual captures.
 
